mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>牙周病学(periodontics) 是口腔医学专业必修课，是研究牙周组织的结构、生理和病理的学科。教学内容主要有牙周组织的应用解剖和生理、牙周病的分类与流行病学、牙周病的病因学与病理机制、牙周病的检查与诊断和治疗、牙周病与全身健康的关系、牙周病学与口腔修复学及正畸学的关系、牙周炎患者的牙种植修复与种植体周病的防治等。<br>牙周病学以理论授课、数字化虚拟仿真教学、实训室仿头模实习和临床见习相结合的方式为主要教学模式。理论授课在传统授课方式的基础上，融合了翻转课堂、小组讨论等线下教学活动，以及超星学习等线上教学活动，以交互、开放的形式实施学生的自主学习和合作学习。课程测评方式以形成性评价和总结性评价相结合。本课程学生学习效果考评由基于表现和能力的过程性评价和总结性评价组成。<br>课程的教学团队由牙周病学教研室多名中青年教师组成，并邀请多名院外知名专家共同参与教学授课；在学生已有的学习基础上，以理论和实践相结合的模式，在培养学生扎实的理论知识、严谨的临床思维、熟练的操作技能的同时，期望学生获得自主学习意识与能力、思辨能力，成为具备科研思维与研究能力的临床口腔医生。</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:70.8500pt;">
                <td width=205 valign=center colspan=4 style="width:123.1000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">课程简介（英文）</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Periodontology is a required course for stomatology majors, focusing on the structure, physiology, and pathology of periodontal tissues. The teaching content primarily covers the applied anatomy and physiology of periodontal tissues, classification and epidemiology of periodontal diseases, etiology and pathological mechanisms, examination, diagnosis, and treatment of periodontal diseases, the relationship between periodontal diseases and systemic health, the interconnections between periodontology and prosthodontics as well as orthodontics, and dental implant restoration in periodontitis patients and the prevention and treatment of peri‑implant diseases.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The primary teaching modes for periodontology combine theoretical lectures, digital virtual simulation teaching, laboratory manikin head practice, and clinical internships. Theoretical lectures are delivered not only through traditional instruction but also integrate offline activities such as flipped classrooms and group discussions, alongside online activities via platforms like Chaoxing Learning, enabling students to engage in autonomous and collaborative learning in an interactive and open manner. Course assessment combines formative and summative evaluation. The student learning outcome evaluation consists of performance‑ and competency‑based process assessment alongside summative assessment.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The teaching team is composed of multiple middle‑aged and young faculty members from the Department of Periodontology, with several renowned external experts invited to co‑teach. Building on students' existing knowledge base and adopting a model that integrates theory with practice, the course aims not only to cultivate solid theoretical knowledge, rigorous clinical reasoning, and proficient operational skills but also to foster students’ capacity for self‑directed learning, critical thinking, and research‑oriented inquiry, ultimately preparing them to become clinically competent stomatologists with scientific research mindset and ability.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
